{"id": "pilot-001", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "I can wait.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "can", "start": 2, "end": 5, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "把重音放在 wait 上，试着把不重读的 can 轻读成 /kən/，再和单独重读的 can 对照。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-002", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "I need to go.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "to", "start": 7, "end": 9, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "重读 need 和 go，让中间的 to 短一点，试试 /tə/。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-003", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Fish and chips, please.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "and", "start": 5, "end": 8, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "把重音放在 Fish 和 chips 上，试着用较短的 /ən/ 读中间的 and。"}, {"text": "Fish and", "start": 0, "end": 8, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "两词间没有停顿时，让 Fish 末尾的 /ʃ/ 自然接上 and 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-004", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "A cup of tea, please.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "of", "start": 6, "end": 8, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先清楚读出 cup 和 tea，再试着把中间不重读的 of 轻读成 /əv/。"}, {"text": "A", "start": 0, "end": 1, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "句首的 A 不强调数量时，可以轻读成 /ə/，把重音放在 cup 上。"}, {"text": "cup of", "start": 2, "end": 8, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "连续读 cup of，两词之间没有停顿时，让 cup 末尾的 /p/ 直接接上 of 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-005", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Come in, please.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "Come in", "start": 0, "end": 7, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先分开读 Come 和 in，再让 Come 末尾的 /m/ 自然接上 in 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-006", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Turn off the light.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "Turn off", "start": 0, "end": 8, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "用同一口气读 Turn off，让 Turn 末尾的 /n/ 自然接上 off 开头的元音。"}, {"text": "the", "start": 9, "end": 12, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "the 在辅音 /l/ 开头的 light 前不重读时，试着短读成 /ðə/。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-007", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Pick it up.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "Pick it", "start": 0, "end": 7, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先慢读 Pick it，再让 Pick 末尾的 /k/ 自然接上 it 开头的元音。"}, {"text": "it up", "start": 5, "end": 10, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先分开读 it 和 up，再不加停顿，让 it 末尾的 /t/ 自然接上 up 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-008", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Hold on a second.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "Hold on", "start": 0, "end": 7, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "用同一口气读 Hold on，让 Hold 末尾的 /d/ 接上 on 开头的元音。"}, {"text": "a", "start": 8, "end": 9, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "a 在 second 前不重读时，可以轻读成 /ə/，把重音放在 second 的第一个音节。"}, {"text": "on a", "start": 5, "end": 9, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "两词之间没有停顿时，让 on 末尾的 /n/ 自然接上 a 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-009", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "I saw her last night.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "last night", "start": 10, "end": 20, "category": "elision", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先读清 last 词尾的 /t/，再试着在连贯快读时省去它，对照两种读法。"}, {"text": "her", "start": 6, "end": 9, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "her 只是指代已知的人、没有对比重音时，试着缩短并弱化元音，再与强调 her 的读法对照。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-010", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "See you next week.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "next week", "start": 8, "end": 17, "category": "elision", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先读出 next 词尾的 /t/，再试着在快读中省去 /t/，直接过渡到 week 的 /w/。"}, {"text": "you", "start": 4, "end": 7, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "普通告别时，如果 you 不重读，可以试试 /jə/，再与强调对方时的完整读法对照。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-011", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "An old man waved at me.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "old man", "start": 3, "end": 10, "category": "elision", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先保留 old 词尾的 /d/，再试着在快读中省去它，感受 /l/ 向 man 开头 /m/ 的过渡。"}, {"text": "An", "start": 0, "end": 2, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "句首的 An 不重读时，可轻读成 /ən/，把注意力放在后面的 old man。"}, {"text": "at", "start": 17, "end": 19, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "at 只引出动作的对象、不承载重音时，试着短读为 /ət/。"}, {"text": "An old", "start": 0, "end": 6, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "两词之间没有停顿时，让 An 末尾的 /n/ 自然接上 old 开头的元音。"}, {"text": "waved at", "start": 11, "end": 19, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "保留 waved 末尾的 /d/，在两词之间没有停顿时，让它接上 at 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-012", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "We walked down the hill.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "walked down", "start": 3, "end": 14, "category": "elision", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先读清 walked 的 /kt/，再试着在较快语流中省去最后的 /t/，保留 /k/ 和 down 的 /d/。"}, {"text": "the", "start": 15, "end": 18, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "the 在 /h/ 开头的 hill 前不重读时，可练习轻短的 /ðə/。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-013", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Did you call me?", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "Did you", "start": 0, "end": 7, "category": "sound_change", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先分别读出末尾的 /d/ 和开头的 /j/，再试试连贯快读时把两音合成 /dʒ/。"}, {"text": "you", "start": 4, "end": 7, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "不强调是你打的电话时，先分开练习较轻的 /jə/，再放回整句听辨。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-014", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Don't you remember?", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "Don't you", "start": 0, "end": 9, "category": "sound_change", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先读清 Don't 末尾的 /t/ 和 you 开头的 /j/，再试试它们在快读中合成 /tʃ/ 的读法。"}, {"text": "you", "start": 6, "end": 9, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "you 不承载对比重音时，可先单独练习较轻的 /jə/，再与重读的 you 对照。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-015", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "About ten people came.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "ten people", "start": 6, "end": 16, "category": "sound_change", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "保留清晰的 /n/ 读一遍，再试着提前合唇，让 people 前面的 /n/ 听起来更接近 [m]。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-016", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "Can I have some water?", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "water", "start": 16, "end": 21, "category": "sound_change", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "练习一种常见美式读法：重读第一个音节，让 /t/ 在进入较轻的第二音节前舌尖轻弹一次 [ɾ]。"}, {"text": "Can", "start": 0, "end": 3, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "在普通请求里，如果 Can 不重读，试着轻读成 /kən/，再用重读的读法对照。"}, {"text": "some", "start": 11, "end": 15, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "当 some 只是表示不定量时，试着轻读成 /səm/，把重音放在 water 上。"}, {"text": "Can I", "start": 0, "end": 5, "category": "linking", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先慢读 Can I，再不加停顿，让 Can 末尾的 /n/ 自然接上 I 开头的元音。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-017", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "I wanna go home.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "wanna", "start": 2, "end": 7, "category": "reduction", "evidence": "text_observed", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "对照 I want to go home 和 I wanna go home，体会口语缩读如何改变节奏。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-018", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "I'm gonna call her.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "gonna", "start": 4, "end": 9, "category": "reduction", "evidence": "text_observed", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "先读 I'm going to call her，再读 I'm gonna call her，对照 going to 的两种说法。"}, {"text": "her", "start": 15, "end": 18, "category": "weak_forms", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "call 后的 her 如果不承载对比重音，可以缩短并弱化元音，再用强调 her 的读法对照。"}]}
{"id": "pilot-019", "source_type": "daily_dialogue", "input_text": "I gotta leave soon.", "review_status": "pending_human_review", "annotations": [{"text": "gotta", "start": 2, "end": 7, "category": "reduction", "evidence": "text_observed", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "用 I have to leave soon 表达同一个意思，再练习例句中带 gotta 的非正式说法。"}, {"text": "gotta", "start": 2, "end": 7, "category": "sound_change", "evidence": "text_candidate", "actual_pronunciation": "uncertain", "speaking_tip_zh": "练习一种常见美式读法：首音节重读、后一音节较轻时，/t/ 可以用舌尖轻弹音 [ɾ] 来读。"}]}
